#: ../../examples/notebooks/03_psf_and_pupils.ipynb:10004
msgid "Telescope pupils are anti-aliased masks; the point-spread function (PSF) is the intensity in the focal plane. The PSF of a uniform circular pupil is the Airy pattern, with its first dark ring at $1.22\\,\\lambda/D$ (Born & Wolf, *Principles of Optics*, §8.5.2)."
msgstr ""

